'''Koro Zuba''' is a [[Nupoid languages|Nupoid language]] of [[Nigeria]]. It is one of several languages which go by the ethnic name [[Jilic languages|Koro]]. However, it has very low (~ 7%) lexical similarity with [[Koro Nulu language|Koro Nulu]] (a.k.a. Koro Ija), which speakers consider to be a variant of the same language (along with [[Jijili language]]) due to ethnic identity,<ref>{{Cite web| title=ISO 639-3 Registration Authority - Request for Change to ISO 639-3 Language Code | url=https://iso639-3.sil.org/sites/iso639-3/files/change_requests/2020/2020-032.pdf | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210422201545/https://iso639-3.sil.org/sites/iso639-3/files/change_requests/2020/2020-032.pdf | archive-date=2021-04-22}}</ref> and instead is closest to [[Dibo language|Dibo]].<ref>{{Cite web| title=Request for New Language Code Element in ISO 639-3 - ISO 639-3 Registration Authority | url=https://iso639-3.sil.org/sites/iso639-3/files/change_requests/2020/2020-032_vkz.pdf | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210422203832/https://iso639-3.sil.org/sites/iso639-3/files/change_requests/2020/2020-032_vkz.pdf | archive-date=2021-04-22}}</ref>

